      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have oculus rift cv1 and have the same problem. It happened after about 1 week of playing. Have tried uninstalling, rebooting and reinstalling vrchat. I also noticed that booting vrchat through the Steam client makes the problem less bad than when I use vrchat with the oculus client. I can barely look at my hand without it disappearing, no matter which world I'm in, or which avatar I use. I am still using the same public avatars I used last week and I'm in the worlds I've been in last week, so there is no way that it's a model/world related issue. I've recalibrated and setup my hardware about 10 times now and it's still not fixed. I am now going to attempt to uninstall everything including the oculus rift driver/client. Maybe that's going to help. I am really sad to not be able to see things, my hands, and people up close anymore.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
